t branch of the Bourbons. The kingdom was the largest sovereign state by population and land area in Italy before the Italian unification, comprising Sicily and most of the area of today's Mezzogiorno (southern Italy) and covering virtually all of the Italian peninsula south of the Papal States.\nThe kingdom was formed when the Kingdom of Sicily merged with the Kingdom of Naples, which was officially also known as the Kingdom of Sicily. Since both kingdoms were named after Sicily, they were collectively known as the \"Two Sicilies\" (Utraque Sicilia, meaning \"both Sicilies\"), and the unified kingdom adopted this name."}],"facts":[{"qid":"Q180393","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q2634","value_label":"Naples","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Naples"},{"qid":"Q180393","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q2656","value_label":"Palermo","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Palermo"},{"qid":"Q180393","kind":"official_language","value_qid":"Q652","value_label":"Italian","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P37","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Italian"},{"qid":"Q180393","kind":"official_language","value_qid":"Q33973","value_label":"Sicilian","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P37","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Sicilian"},{"qid":"Q180393","kind":"official_language","value_qid":"Q33845","value_label":"Neapolitan language","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P37","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Neapolitan language"},{"qid":"Q180393","kind":"language","value_qid":"Q33973","value_label":"Sicilian","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P2936","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Sicilian"},{"qid":"Q180393","kind":"official_religion","value_qid":"Q1841","value_label":"Catholicism","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P3075","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Catholicism"},{"qid":"Q180393","kind":"government","value_qid":"Q184