m 1191 until his death. From 1194, he was also King of Sicily as the husband and co-ruler of Queen Constance I.\nHenry was the second son of Emperor Frederick Barbarossa and Beatrice I, Countess of Burgundy. Well educated in the Latin language, as well as Roman and canon law, he was also a patron of poets and a skilled poet himself. In 1186, he married Constance of Sicily.","image":"Codex Manesse Heinrich VI. (HRR).jpg","birth":1165.8328767123287,"death":1197.7397260273972},"Q332717":{"label":"Ferdinand II of the Two Sicilies","description":"King of the Two sicilies","enwiki":"Ferdinand II of the Two Sicilies","summary":"Ferdinand II (Italian: Ferdinando Carlo Maria; Sicilian: Ferdinannu Carlu Maria; Neapolitan: Ferdinando Carlo Maria; 12 January 1810 –  22 May 1859) was King of the Two Sicilies from 1830 until his death in 1859.","image":"Raffaele Messina - Ferdinando II in abito di San Gennaro a Palazzo Reale con eruzione del Vesuvio sullo sfondo 1832.jpg","birth":1810.0301369863014,"death":1859.386301369863}},"media":{"Flag of the Kingdom of the Two Sicilies (1816) (Sodacan style).svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Flag_of_the_Kingdom_of_the_Two_Sicilies_%281816%29_%28Sodacan_style%29.svg/330px-Flag_of_the_Kingdom_of_the_Two_Sicilies_%281816%29_%28Sodacan_style%29.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Kingdom_of_the_Two_Sicilies_(1816)_(Sodacan_style).svg","author":"Original:  Flopao\nDerivative work:  ZuppaDiCarlo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},"CoA Kingdom of the Two Sicilies.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/CoA_Kingdom_of_the_Two_Sicilies.svg/330px-CoA_Kingdom_of_the_Two_Sicilies.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CoA_Kingdom_of_the_Two_Sicilies.svg","author":"Flopao","license":"CC BY-SA 